            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0096" n="12" xml:id="pg12"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/2925</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sulzer</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Minister of Switzerland,
                    in charge of German interests in the United States, and has the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of his memoranda<anchor n="1" xml:id="d17-f1"/> of
                    September 25, 1917, and August 11, 1917, in regard to granting permission for
                    wives of German prisoners interned in the United States to visit their husbands
                    on stated occasions.</p>
                <p>The Secretary of State has the honor to inform the Minister of Switzerland that
                    the following provision has now been made by the Department of War in the
                    premises: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Prisoners of war will be allowed to receive visitors, under such
                            restrictions as may be considered necessary by the commanding officer of
                            the camp or barracks in which they are interned, on one day each
                            week.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-09"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">October 9, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
